program in object-code form through the Apple App Store: compliance with the
Apple App Store terms of service is not to be considered a further restriction
under section 7 with respect to material whose copyright is held by Mirana
Technologies Inc., and Mirana Technologies Inc. will not treat App Store
distribution of official builds as a violation of the license with respect to
that material.


WHAT THIS PERMISSION DOES NOT COVER
-----------------------------------

Read this part. It is the reason this file exists as prose rather than as a
paragraph nobody reads.

Section 7 permits an additional permission only over material for which the
grantor can give copyright permission. **This permission therefore covers only
material copyrighted by Mirana Technologies Inc. It does not, and cannot,
extend to third-party components.**

The most important of those is **libsignal** (Copyright Signal Messenger, LLC),
which is licensed AGPL-3.0-only and is linked by the iOS application, the
command-line client, and the server's authentication function. Signal granted
an App Store additional permission once, in June 2016, for the now-archived
`libsignal-protocol-c` under GPLv3. That grant was never carried forward to the
current libsignal, whose README states that use outside of Signal is
unsupported. **There is no current permission from Signal to rely on.**

Consequently this file is not a complete answer to the GPL-family/App Store
question for a binary containing libsignal. It resolves that question only for
Mirana's own code. That residual risk was weighed deliberately and accepted
in writing on 2026-07-27, in the project's internal licensing record, by
Mirana Technologies Inc. — the party able to act on it.

Anyone redistributing a modified version should reach their own conclusion
rather than inheriting ours.


CONTRIBUTIONS
-------------

This permission can only be granted over code the project holds the rights to.
Contributions are accepted on the terms in CONTRIBUTING.md, which include the
same grant — because a single merged contribution without it makes this
permission unretrofittable without tracing every contributor, which is a
multi-year problem and not a paperwork one.
